cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "hele-shaw-cells-example: a blueprint-aligned NFDI4Ing Hele-Shaw cells benchmark"
abstract: >-
  hele-shaw-cells-example is the blueprint-aligned instance repository for the
  Hele-Shaw cells benchmark of the NFDI4IngModelValidationPlatform. It
  contains a 2D OpenFOAM-v2112 simulation of radial viscous fingering in a
  circular Hele-Shaw cell, where air injected at the centre displaces a
  viscous soap solution. The interface is captured with the Volume-of-Fluid
  method using the isoAdvector scheme; the surface-tension force is modelled
  with the continuum-surface-force approach. Three parameter configurations
  (reference, mesh refinement, flow-rate variation) form a minimal
  convergence + sensitivity study. The Docker image, solver, mesh, fluid
  properties, and numerics are identical to the hele-shaw-cells-runnable
  reference build; only the repository layout follows the platform's
  instance-repo schema (parameters_*.json, top-level Snakefile, RO-Crate
  provenance, metrics smoke test).
